From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:01:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 053/148] hjviewer: ui: mobile-settings: grouped cards for the
 phone settings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The phone's Settings tab and its display defaults page were settings_ui's
flat Android list on Android (18 px rows, blue section titles, the system
font) and its plain iOS list on an iPhone. Both now use one grouped look:

- the canvas behind (the dark theme's surface), each section a card
  (hjvCardDecoration) under a small grey title, settings_ui's iOS rows
  inside in the palette's colours: 16 px titles in Pretendard, 22 px
  outlined icons in textSecondary, inset dividers, values at the row's
  end in textSecondary (capped so a long one wraps instead of running
  past the card), Cupertino switches in the primary colour.
- Off an iPhone a switch row still toggles from anywhere on it, as the
  Android row did. The fingerprint moves under its row, where its 64
  digits fit; the trusted devices' delete button is no longer white on
  the light app bar.

Behaviour, texts and keys are unchanged.

After an independent review (screens in light and dark, the diff, the code rules):

- A tile's description (the fingerprint, the 프로젝트TF notice, the
  recording directory) sits under its title inside the row: it takes the
  row's tap and press colour (a tap on the fingerprint's digits copies it
  again, as upstream's Android row did), starts at the title's edge and
  gets the row's inset divider, and settings_ui no longer rounds the next
  row in the middle of a card. An empty fingerprint shows no description.
- In a section with icons a row without one keeps the icon's room, so the
  Settings card has one text edge and one divider inset; the value cap
  counts that room only in such sections.
- Off an iPhone rows are 48 px high, Android's touch target; on an iPhone
  they stay 44.
- The pickers (view style, image quality, codec, keep screen on) are
  navigation rows that end in the app's chevron after their value
  (settings_ui's own is a CupertinoIcons glyph, a font the app does not
  bundle); a picker that cannot be opened shows none.
- Row icons and the account avatar are 24 px, on the icon scale.

Behaviour, texts and keys are unchanged.

